  detail=["Token-aware wrappers per library; warm set versus on-demand per D65.", "uPlot live chart on `useLive` append mode; set and measure the target rate (at least 60 updates per second with 10k points on CI hardware).", "License and version re-verification recorded in VERIFIED_FACTS.", "Team components (KT-11, D121): presence avatars, live cursors, a respondent tracker and attribution chips, built on WP-31's hooks, reading the tokens and accepting `className` (KT-10).", "From WP-31 (D168, INTERFACES §2.3): `useRespondents()` gives `self`, and under the manifest's `team.visibility` `counts` and `complete` (`counts`) or every `Respondent` (`names`), each with `status` (`not-opened`, `drafting`, `submitted`) and `openedAt`/`submittedAt`; `usePresence({ cursor?, selection? })` gives `others` (`PresencePeer`: `cursor` in document coordinates, `selection` as a `data-presence-id`, `id` or `name`) and `count`; an artifact-scoped field's `meta.updatedBy` is `{ kind, name?, key?, self?, at? }`. A person's `key` (`vk_…`) is the same in all three, so a chip, an avatar and a cursor of one person match. Components render what the hook gives for the visibility in force and nothing more (`private` shows only the viewer's own entry), and draw on `status: \"unavailable\"` (outside a live page, and in `verify`) without data. The fixtures of `packages/runtime/test/fixtures/artifacts/team` and `tests/e2e/fixtures/team` show each shape."],
